  <article class="app-card research-project" id="asl-stem">
    <div class="app-content">
      <div class="small-label">University of Washington · Research</div>
      <h3><a href="https://aslstem.cs.washington.edu/">ASL-STEM ↗</a></h3>
      <p>I worked on ASL-STEM at UW under Professor Emeritus Richard Ladner.</p>

      <p>A community-built dictionary of American Sign Language vocabulary for science, technology, engineering, and mathematics. It helps Deaf students and scientists communicate about technical concepts that lack widely established signs.</p>
      <p>ASL users can share signs for the same concept across regions, helping the community develop shared vocabulary and making STEM education and careers more accessible.</p>
      <p>The collection now holds <strong>8,721+ STEM terms</strong> and <strong>3,265+ community-contributed sign videos</strong>.</p>
      <a class="research-about" href="https://aslstem.cs.washington.edu/about">About the project ↗</a>
    </div>
